# Python and tooling
.venv/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Editors and OS
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# Secrets: .env holds a real API key; local variants (.env.local ...) are ignored too.
# .env.example (empty values) stays tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# Raw data stays local (WESAD alone is 3.8 GB and may not be redistributed), except the
# two small public files the app needs to build the environment trace on a fresh clone:
# ISS EDA RR-1 cabin telemetry (NASA OSDR) and MSL-RAD Mars surface dose (NASA PDS).
data/raw/*
!data/raw/eda/
data/raw/eda/*
!data/raw/eda/RR-1_telemetry.csv
!data/raw/radlab/
data/raw/radlab/*
!data/raw/radlab/MSL-RAD_Mars_2017-09-04_to_09-18.csv

# WESAD (academic, non-commercial use; cite Schmidt et al. 2018): only the fitted summary
# parameters are committed; the per-subject, per-minute series stays local (re-running the
# analysis needs WESAD downloaded first).
data/processed/wesad_hr_hrv.csv
# The raw-data inspection report quotes rows and statistics of every raw file, WESAD included.
data/inspect_report.md

# Engine results: the full-profile cache is committed so a fresh clone shows the demo
# results at once, offline. Local-profile runs, and runs on a clone without the WESAD series
# (file names carry "wesad_params"), stay local. Before a commit remove stale full-profile
# files with: python scripts/prune_cache.py --delete   (add --all to clear local runs too)
cache/*
!cache/*_full_*.json
cache/*_wesad_params_*.json

*.log

# Video output (video/record.py cuts the shots into video/clips/)
video/*.srt
video/*.mp3
video/*.mp4
video/build/
video/clips/
# photos for the video (third-party licences; sources in docs/submission_links.md)
video/assets/

# Working documents kept local (docs/ also covers docs/screenshots/)
docs/
CLAUDE.md
